# Raw nflverse play-by-play is NOT committed.
#
# 40 MB of third-party data (nflverse, CC-BY 4.0) that anyone can re-download
# from the nflverse-data GitHub release. Committing it would bloat every clone
# and every CI checkout to carry bytes that are trivially regenerated.
#
# Retrieve with:
#   python -c "import urllib.request; ..."  # see the header of
#   intelligence/props/sgp_correlation_estimator.py, which downloads on demand
#   and names this directory.
#
# The DERIVED artifact IS committed: data/snapshots/sgp_correlations.json (a few
# KB, the measured matrix) is the thing consumers read, and it carries its own
# provenance. The corpus is an input; the estimate is the result.
#
# Scoped .gitignore rather than a line in the root .gitignore, following the
# precedent in data/backtest/.gitignore: AGENTS.md law 2 puts .gitignore under
# "never modify", and a directory-scoped file is the narrower, safer mechanism.
# One commit, reversible, affects nothing else in the tree.
pbp/
